DIFF 4 — the one new capability: a file's mtime
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

runtime/avra_runtime.c — beside avra_io_kind, which already stats:

+// The path's modification time in seconds, or -errno.
+int64_t avra_io_modified(const char* path) {
+    struct stat st;
+    if (stat(path, &st) != 0) return -errno;
+    return (int64_t)st.st_mtime;
+}

  + its row in the runtime registry (features/facts.av's `rt_sigs`),
    answering an int, arguments borrowed — a C body that keeps nothing.

packages/std-io/src/io.av:

+/// When the path was last written, in seconds. A path the host will
+/// not describe reads as 0, which is older than everything — so a
+/// missing source rebuilds rather than being skipped.
+export fn modified(path: string) -> int {
+    let t = avra_io_modified(path)
+    if t < 0 { return 0 }
+    t
+}

  NOTE the empty case, written first: 0 means "older than everything",
  so an unreadable source triggers a rebuild instead of a skip. The
  other polarity silently ships a stale object.

  `Host` (workspace.av:29) does NOT need a fifth field: the freshness
  question is asked in the CLI, which has @std/io directly. Keep the
  Host at four.

