THE THREE THINGS TO PROBE BEFORE WRITING THIS
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  1. `n?.sources` on a nullable struct field answering a `List<string>`
     — the diff above avoids it with an explicit `if n == null`, on the
     strength of CLAUDE.md's warning that an empty literal does not
     adopt a nullable aggregate want. Probe it; if `n?.sources ?? []`
     compiles, the two helpers collapse to one line each.
  2. `.all(step_done(it))` where the predicate has a side effect —
     short-circuit is wanted here (a failed step stops the rest), but
     confirm `all` is lazy and does not walk the whole list first.
  3. `Exit` — read one code out of it the way `judged_link` does, not
     a second spelling.
